# Meran

## Lore

Merans are the merfolk of sailors'' stories: a humanoid torso on the body and tail of a fish. Males run to blues, greens and grays with yellow, red or black markings; females are brighter, in whites, yellows, oranges and pale greens marked with dark red, purple or blue. For a limited time a Meran can trade the tail for legs and walk ashore as a scaled fish-person, or, for a shorter time still, pass as an ordinary human or Lemurian.

They have lived in the deep ocean for thousands of years and kept themselves out of history on purpose. They are curious about other peoples but careful, preferring to watch from a distance or in disguise, and they trust almost no outsiders. The Lemurians are the great exception: the two peoples treat each other as family and are rarely found apart.

A Meran is brave, principled and devoted to the sea, and most live simply as hunters, gatherers and undersea farmers. The one thing a Meran cannot do without is seawater.

## GM Notes

Also known as Mermaids, Mermen and Merfolk. The stat block is headed as an optional player character or NPC.

Size: 6 feet (1.8 m) of body plus a tail of 1D4+3 feet (1.2 to 2.1 m); 6 feet +1D6 inches in Lemurian or human form. Weight 200-270 lbs (90 to 121.5 kg). Average life span 1D6x10+100 years. One live young is born underwater; the land forms seldom show before age three or four.

Nobody outside the two races knows whether Merans are aliens, a native species or an offshoot of Lemuria. Their small kingdom, ruled by Queen Jennara for the last 50 years, lies among the drowned islands of what was French Polynesia; villages commonly hold 1D4x1,000 people in stone dwellings underwater. Their numbers have fallen sharply since the Lord of the Deep appeared.

Habitat: all oceans, mainly the Pacific and Indian, avoiding the Mid-Atlantic because of the Minions of Splugorth. Thousands have settled on other ocean worlds.

Allies: Lemurians above all; whales, dolphins and Sea Druids are friends, Ichthyleans friendly rivals. Amphibs, Junk Crabs, the New Navy and other outsiders are met with suspicion but not enmity; human Tritonians are disliked and distrusted. Enemies: the Naut''Yll first, then the Minions of Splugorth, the Lord of the Deep and his minions, Davey Jones, the Milu undead, demons, and anyone who threatens Merans, Lemuria or the oceans.
